# couchd stage 2 - the ONE thing ds2000 may do as root without a password.
#
# Install as /etc/sudoers.d/couchd (mode 0440, root:root) and ONLY via
# visudo -c -f: a syntax error in sudoers.d locks the box out of sudo.
#
#   sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g root sudoers-couchd /etc/sudoers.d/couchd
#   sudo visudo -c
#
# SR3: rollback must not need a password at 11pm. The scope is one
# root-owned, root-only-writable script, so this grants exactly "put the pad
# back" and nothing else. If the script were writable by ds2000 this line
# would be a root shell - INSTALL.md's verification step checks that.
#
# The trailing "" is load-bearing and is NOT an empty placeholder. An
# earlier version of this file omitted it and claimed the script "takes no
# arguments on purpose, so there is no way to turn it into a general-purpose
# root shell". That reasoning was wrong twice over. First, a command spec
# with no argument list permits ANY arguments - sudo only restricts
# arguments when you write them down, so the old line would have run
# `couchd-input-release --anything` just as happily. Second, the safety was
# never coming from the argument list anyway: it comes from the script being
# root-owned and root-only-writable at a fixed absolute path, so ds2000
# cannot change what runs. `""` is sudo's way of spelling "no arguments at
# all", and it is here so that the file's stated scope and its actual
# grant are the same thing - if the script ever grows an argument, this
# line must be edited deliberately rather than silently permitting it.
#
# One more dependency worth writing down: the script's root-privileged body
# resolves systemctl, mv, udevadm and sed. It sets its own PATH for that
# reason, but sudo's `secure_path` (Defaults secure_path=... in
# /etc/sudoers, on by default on Debian/Ubuntu) is the outer guarantee that
# a caller-controlled PATH never reaches root here. If secure_path is ever
# removed from this box's sudoers, the script's own PATH line becomes the
# only thing standing between ds2000's environment and a root shell -
# do not delete it.
#
ds2000 ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/couchd-input-release ""
